    },
    "body": "## Summary\n- never pass a null text search filter into the public job discovery repository query\n- use an explicit empty-string sentinel in JPQL so PostgreSQL/Hibernate keeps the parameter text-typed\n- cover missing and whitespace-only search filters in JobService tests\n- add a PostgreSQL runtime smoke for `GET /jobs` without `query` and with a blank `query`\n\n## Bug reproduced locally\nThe previous query could bind a null `String` search parameter as `bytea` under Hibernate 7/PostgreSQL, causing `ERROR: function lower(bytea) does not exist` when the public jobs page loaded without a text filter.\n\n## Merge gate\nDo not merge until API verify, web verify and the full container/runtime smoke all pass, including the new job-discovery regression step.",
